     Media type. Resources MUST be served as application/wow+json, a working name that stays provisional until the group decides it. It is JSON, and its fragment identifiers are JSON Pointers (RFC 6901, section 6). application/json MUST stay available by content negotiation.\n\n\
     Entity tags. GET /wow/world, GET /wow/spatial/{spatialID} and the node GET MUST return ETag and Last-Modified, and MUST answer a matching If-None-Match with 304. The node PUT and DELETE MUST honor If-Match and MUST answer 412, changing nothing, when it does not match (RFC 9110).\n\n\
-    Cross-origin access. Responses MUST carry Access-Control-Allow-Origin as the world's policy allows, and Access-Control-Expose-Headers: ETag. Preflight responses MUST allow the methods GET, HEAD, POST, PUT and DELETE, and the request headers Authorization, Content-Type, If-None-Match and If-Match."
+    Cross-origin access. Responses MUST carry Access-Control-Allow-Origin as the world's policy allows, and Access-Control-Expose-Headers: ETag. Preflight responses MUST allow the methods GET, HEAD, POST, PUT and DELETE, and the request headers Authorization, Content-Type, If-None-Match and If-Match.\n\n\
+    Events. A world that offers an event stream MUST list it in the World resource under services.events, relative to the world's base URL. It carries user_joined, user_left, node_created, node_updated and node_deleted. As simpleWorlds sends them, user_joined carries user (the User), user_left carries userId, node_created and node_updated carry node (the Node), and node_deleted carries nodeId. Each event MUST carry type, revision (this world's count of its changes, one higher for each), time (the server's UTC time of the change, in RFC 3339 form) and urls (every resource whose representation changed, relative to the base: the User for a user event, the node and every ancestor that embeds it for a node event, and wow/world, which reports the revision), as the Event schema lists them. The revision MUST survive restarts, and World.revision reports the current one. A write that changes nothing MUST NOT produce a revision or an event. A client MAY resume with since=<revision>. A world that can no longer replay from there MUST send resync with its current revision, and the client MUST then re-read.\n\n\
+    Stream authentication. A world MAY require authorization for its stream. The token MUST then be the stream's first message, the JSON text {\"type\": \"auth\", \"token\": \"<access token>\"}. The token MUST NOT appear in a URL. The world MUST close a stream without a valid token within 5 seconds. A world MUST refuse a stream from an origin its policy does not allow.\n\n\
+    Data points. A data point is a resource URL with a JSON Pointer fragment (RFC 6901, section 6), such as {base}wow/spatial/1/node/42#/properties/temperature. The pointer MUST NOT pass through children: a child is named by its own node URL. Reading, conditional reading and subscribing MUST NOT create a user."
